<title>BELGIUM: EU oilseeds plantings below Blair House limit.</title>
<headline>EU oilseeds plantings below Blair House limit.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-01-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Union's oilseed plantings did not exceed the bilateral Blair House agreement with the U.S., the cereals management committee was told on Thursday, an EU official said Friday.</p>
<p>&quot;The figures were presented by the Commission and no penalties will apply for producers,&quot; the offcial said.</p>
<p>Under the 1992 Blair House agreement EU subsidised oilseed plantings cannot exceed 5.482 million hectares, less ten percent compulsory set-aside.</p>
</text>
